+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional due date (date only); API and list page show and filter overdue todos.
+
+**Architecture:** `TodoStore` stores `Todo` with `DueDate` and owns the single overdue rule (via an
+injected `TimeProvider`, "today" in UTC) plus the overdue filter. `Program.cs` maps store results to
+a response record `TodoView` that adds the computed `Overdue`. `Home.razor` asks the store for the
+(optionally filtered) list and renders due date, overdue hint and a "nur überfällige" checkbox.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor Web App (interactive server), minimal APIs, System.Text.Json, xUnit,
+`WebApplicationFactory<Program>`.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-due-date-design.md` (Ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages (`TimeProvider` is in the BCL; the fake clock is a hand-written test class).
+- Validation errors → HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}` via the existing middleware in `Program.cs`.
+- TDD: failing test first, in `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/`.
+- Every new UI element gets a `data-testid`: `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `filter-overdue`.
+- Overdue = not done AND `DueDate` is set AND `DueDate` < today's date in **UTC**. Due today → not overdue.
+- JSON: `dueDate` as `"YYYY-MM-DD"` or `null`; `overdue` bool. Display date format `dd.MM.yyyy`.
+- Exact UI copy: `fällig <dd.MM.yyyy>`, `überfällig`, checkbox label `nur überfällige`.
+- No styling.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. Invalid `dueDate` (`"2026-02-30"`, `"20.11.2026"`) on POST and PATCH → 400 and no change to the store — Task 2 tests.
+2. PATCH with only `title`/`done` must keep an existing `dueDate` (absent ≠ null) — Task 1 and Task 2 tests.
+3. Boundaries: due today → not overdue; due yesterday but done → not overdue; no date → never — Task 1 test.
+4. "Today" must be UTC even if the clock reports a non-UTC offset (`2026-11-12T23:30-02:00` is the 13th in UTC) — Task 1 test.
+5. `GET /todos?overdue=abc` → 400, not 500 or an unfiltered list — Task 2 test.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — due date, overdue rule, patch semantics, filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`
+- Create: `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/FixedClock.cs`
+- Modify: `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces:
+  - `public record Todo(int Id, string Title, bool Done, DateOnly? DueDate = null);`
+  - `public record NewTodo(string? Title, DateOnly? DueDate = null);`
+  - `public class TodoPatch` with ctors `TodoPatch()` and `TodoPatch(string? title, bool? done)`,
+    settable `Title`, `Done`, `DueDate`, and `[JsonIgnore] bool DueDateSpecified` (see Step 3).
+  - `TodoStore()` (uses `TimeProvider.System`) and `TodoStore(TimeProvider clock)`.
+  - `DateOnly TodoStore.Today` — `DateOnly.FromDateTime(clock.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime)`.
+  - `bool TodoStore.IsOverdue(Todo todo)`.
+  - `IReadOnlyList<Todo> TodoStore.List(bool overdueOnly = false)`.
+  - Test helper `sealed class FixedClock(DateTimeOffset now) : TimeProvider` overriding `GetUtcNow()`.
+
